# mxr-phone authorized_keys entry — SITE CONFIG, one line per device.
# Paste into ~/.ssh/authorized_keys on the Mini (as jefe), replacing:
#   * <PHONE-TAILNET-IP>: the phone's tailnet address (Tailscale admin / `tailscale status`
#     — e.g. iphone171 = 100.73.71.78). `from=` makes a COPIED key useless from any other
#     device, even inside the tailnet (design H4).
#   * <SHORTCUTS-ED25519-PUBKEY>: from the iPhone — Shortcuts app > any "Run Script Over
#     SSH" action > Authentication: SSH Key > tap the key > Copy Public Key. The private
#     key never leaves the phone.
# `restrict` denies pty/port-forwarding/agent-forwarding/X11/user-rc wholesale; the forced
# command means EVERY session runs mxr-phone regardless of what the client requests.
# ONE key per device, comment-tagged with the date; revocation = delete the line
# (+ remove the device in the Tailscale admin — two independent locks, design §7).
restrict,from="<PHONE-TAILNET-IP>",command="/Users/jefe/.myndaix/bin/mxr-phone" ssh-ed25519 <SHORTCUTS-ED25519-PUBKEY> iphone-2026-09
